.com/angular/angular/issues/36672#issuecomment-634305479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/36672","id":634305479,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzNDMwNTQ3OQ==","user":{"login":"AndrewKushnir","id":43554145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTU0MTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43554145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir","html_url":"https://github.com/AndrewKushnir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AndrewKushnir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-05-26T22:05:34Z","updated_at":"2020-05-26T22:05:34Z","body":"Hi @edusoccer1121, thanks for providing a repro. According to the type definition of the `patchValue` method here:\r\nhttps://github.com/angular/angular/blob/a62c1c441c67616ce5eacc7e8dcfe169316d4552/packages/forms/src/model.ts#L1470\r\nthe `null` and `undefined` values (that you try to use as an argument) are not supported and should actually trigger a TypeScript error. I've updated your repro ([new repro is available here](https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-issue-repro2-wqymqe?file=src/app/app.component.ts)) to set an explicit type for the `errorFormValue` field and now you can see that the TypeScript error is produced. It looks like Framework works as expected and no additional handling inside the `patchValue` fu